#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:7
msgid "Ubuntu (binary)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:11
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:13
msgid ""
"This page explains how to install ROS 2 on Ubuntu Linux from a pre-built "
"binary package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:17
msgid ""
"The pre-built binary does not include all ROS 2 packages. All packages in "
"the `ROS base variant <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#ros-base>`_ "
"are included, and only a subset of packages in the `ROS desktop variant "
"<https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#desktop-variants>`_ are included. "
"The exact list of packages are described by the repositories listed in `this "
"ros2.repos file <https://github.com/ros2/ros2/blob/rolling/ros2.repos>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:21
msgid "There are also :doc:`deb packages <../Ubuntu-Install-Debs>` available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:24
msgid "System requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:26
msgid ""
"We currently support Ubuntu Resolute (26.04) 64-bit x86 and 64-bit ARM. The "
"Rolling Ridley distribution will change target platforms from time to time "
"as new platforms are selected for development. Most people will want to use "
"a stable ROS distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:31
msgid "System setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:34
msgid "Set locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:5
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``POSIX``. We test with the following settings. "
"However, it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported "
"locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:10
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install locales\n"
"$ sudo locale-gen en_US en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ sudo update-locale LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:39
msgid "Enable required repositories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:5
msgid "You will need to add the ROS 2 apt repository to your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:7
msgid ""
"First ensure that the `Ubuntu Universe repository <https://help.ubuntu.com/"
"community/Repositories/Ubuntu>`_ is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:9
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install software-properties-common\n"
"$ sudo add-apt-repository universe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:14
msgid ""
"The `ros-apt-source <https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/"
">`_ packages provide keys and apt source configuration for the various ROS "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:16
msgid ""
"Installing the ros2-apt-source package will configure ROS 2 repositories for "
"your system. Updates to repository configuration will occur automatically "
"when new versions of this package are released to the ROS repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install curl -y\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk -"
"F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ curl -L -o /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb \"https://github.com/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/"
"ros2-apt-source_${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}.$(. /etc/os-release && echo "
"${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-${VERSION_CODENAME}})_all.deb\"\n"
"$ sudo dpkg -i /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:44
msgid "Install prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:46
msgid ""
"There are a few packages that must be installed in order to get and unpack "
"the binary release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:48
msgid "$ sudo apt install tar bzip2 wget -y"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:53
msgid "Install development tools (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:55
msgid ""
"If you are going to build ROS packages or otherwise do development, you can "
"also install the development tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:57
msgid "$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install ros-dev-tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:62
msgid "Install ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:64
msgid ""
"Binary releases of Rolling Ridley are not provided. Instead you may download "
"nightly :ref:`prerelease binaries <Prerelease_binaries>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:67
msgid ""
"Download the latest package for Ubuntu; let's assume that it ends up at ``~/"
"Downloads/ros2-package-linux-x86_64.tar.bz2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:69
msgid ""
"Note: there may be more than one binary download option which might cause "
"the file name to differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:72
msgid "Unpack it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:74
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ tar xf ~/Downloads/ros2-package-linux-x86_64.tar.bz2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:83
msgid "Install dependencies using rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Upgrade-Admonition.rst:5
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages are built on frequently updated Ubuntu systems. It is always "
"recommended that you ensure your system is up to date before installing new "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Upgrade-Admonition.rst:8
msgid "$ sudo apt upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:87
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt install -y python3-rosdep\n"
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/share --ignore-src -"
"y --skip-keys \"cyclonedds fastcdr fastdds iceoryx_binding_c rmw_connextdds "
"rti-connext-dds-7.7.0 urdfdom_headers\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_rosdep_Linux_Mint.rst:5
msgid ""
"**Note**: If you're using a distribution that is based on Ubuntu (like Linux "
"Mint) but does not identify itself as such, you'll get an error message like "
"``Unsupported OS [mint]``. In this case append ``--os=ubuntu:resolute`` to "
"the above command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:98
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:100
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at runtime. See the :doc:`guide <../RMW-"
"Implementations/Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work "
"with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:104
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:106
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:108
msgid "$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:114
msgid ""
"Replace ``.bash`` with your shell if you're not using bash. Possible values "
"are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:118
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:120
msgid "In one terminal, source the setup file and then run a C++ ``talker``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:122
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:127
msgid ""
"In another terminal source the setup file and then run a Python ``listener``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:129
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:134
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:139
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:141
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:144
msgid "Troubleshoot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:146
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting techniques can be found :doc:`here <../Installation-"
"Troubleshooting>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:149
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:151
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:154
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Install-Binary.rst:156
msgid "$ rm -rf ~/ros2_rolling"
msgstr ""
